# d) or of aggregate computed during optimization. Actually
# there is no way to test this, indeed,
# 'explain select max(t3.a) from t3;'
# does use "Select tables optimized away", but when it is put into a
# correlated subquery, not everything can be computed during optimization
# (due to the outer reference) so the subquery gets AGGR_REGULAR and
# continues into full-blown optimization. 
explain select max(t3.a) from t3;
